WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.440
With ten years of cinematic backstory and&nbsp;
an endless comic history to draw from,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:08.800
every character in the MCU is&nbsp;
worth following by the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.840
Marvel's Infinity Saga wraps up — but some&nbsp;
receive more satisfying conclusions than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.240
others. From cosmic villains to genius,&nbsp;
billionaire, playboy philanthropists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.400
here are the Avengers: Endgame character&nbsp;
endings ranked from worst to best.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.000
While each member of the Black Order gets a&nbsp;
pretty epic ending in Avengers: Infinity War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.200
once you get to Endgame, the group stumbles a bit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.080
As their 2014 selves face off against the&nbsp;
Avengers, each of them goes out not with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.080
bang but with a whimper. Ebony Maw attempts to&nbsp;
reclaim Iron Man's Infinity Gauntlet but fails,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:47.760
Corvus Glaive is quickly stabbed and tossed aside&nbsp;
by Okoye, and Cull Obsidian is unceremoniously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.080
crushed to death by a giant Ant-Man. Their&nbsp;
endings are inconsequential, to say the least.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.360
Despite receiving her own solo film&nbsp;
between Infinity War and Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.520
Captain Marvel ended up playing a pretty&nbsp;
minor role in the grand finale. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.800
she does manage to stay busy, saving Tony Stark&nbsp;
and Nebula in the opening moments of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.160
and then arriving in the nick of&nbsp;
time to join in the final battle.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:13.680
But when it comes to the character's&nbsp;
ending, it isn't too glamorous.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:19.200
Carol Danvers is last seen paying her respects&nbsp;
at Stark's funeral as the film wraps up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.280
She looks a bit out of place, which makes&nbsp;
sense considering she barely knew Tony.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:27.520
The lackluster ending to her undercooked&nbsp;
story lands her pretty low on our list.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.853
While practically every hero in the galaxy&nbsp;
is present at the final fight in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.853 --> 00:01:37.760
Endgame, the armies of Wakanda provide a sea of&nbsp;
muscle to back up the Avengers and their allies.

00:01:37.760 --> 00:01:42.400
Standing tall at the head of the well-trained&nbsp;
African army are two characters who deserve a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:48.720
shoutout Okoye and Shuri. Okoye makes her mark&nbsp;
on the proceedings by taking out Corvus Glaive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.600
single-handedly, while Shuri can briefly be&nbsp;
seen blasting away opponents on the battlefield.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:58.000
But after their splashy entrance, they mostly&nbsp;
fade into the background of the final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.840
making their collective "ending" a bit&nbsp;
less impressive than we might've hoped.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.720
Iron Man's bittersweet ending wouldn't&nbsp;
feel complete without seeing how it affects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.760
the people closest to him: Pepper Potts,&nbsp;
Morgan Stark, and, of course, Happy Hogan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:16.080
Appropriately, the trio takes the emotional&nbsp;
spotlight in the fading moments of the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.720
beginning with Tony's final holographic message.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.960
After donning her Rescue armor in the film's&nbsp;
final battle and comforting her husband in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:27.520
his last moments, Pepper's last scene&nbsp;
sees her bidding adieu to her lost love&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:33.280
as she sets Tony's arc reactor adrift on the lake.&nbsp;
Meanwhile, Happy and Morgan have a touching moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.520
on the porch, where Tony's daughter shows&nbsp;
that she's inherited her father's appetite.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.040
"I want an American cheeseburger."

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:39.600
"You hungry?"

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.680
"Mmhmm."

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:42.180
"What do you want?"

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.320
"Cheeseburgers."

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.720
Fondly remembering his former boss, Happy promises&nbsp;
Morgan as many burgers as she could ever want.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:55.280
It's a sweet, fitting goodbye for the people&nbsp;
closest to the Infinity Saga's biggest hero.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.320
James Rhodes, a.k.a. War Machine,&nbsp;
has faithfully remained by Tony&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:05.280
Stark's side throughout the entire MCU. The&nbsp;
character stays busy throughout Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.680
and his story technically wraps up on the&nbsp;
lakeside as he attends Stark's funeral.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.480
However, the most emotional part of James&nbsp;
Rhodes' ending occurs a few moments earlier.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.840
In the seconds after Tony Stark snaps away Thanos&nbsp;
and his army, Rhodey is the first one to find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.960
his best friend as he breathes his last. As he&nbsp;
realizes what's taking place, he puts his hand to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:30.560
Tony's head, and the two brothers in arms share a&nbsp;
quiet moment together. The scene is deeply moving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.560
especially considering what the pair of friends&nbsp;
have gone through up to that point in time.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.200
Peter Parker gets tangled up in&nbsp;
the Thanos storyline early on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:43.200
when Ebony Maw's giant flying donut&nbsp;
parks right over his hometown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.400
From there, the web-head joins Stark and&nbsp;
Dr. Strange on an unplanned trip to Titan.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.360
At the end of Infinity War, Parker is tragically&nbsp;
snapped away, and he doesn't reappear until the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.840
portals open up in the climactic ending of&nbsp;
Endgame. No worse for wear after his five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:02.720
years as dust, the Crime-stopper from Queens&nbsp;
swings right back into action and even carries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.840
Stark's Infinity Gauntlet for a bit. He mourns&nbsp;
the loss of his mentor when Stark dies and has a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.640
place of honor at the funeral. However, his ending&nbsp;
gets a little brighter when he's shown reuniting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:18.280
with his friend, Ned, setting the stage for his&nbsp;
own solo sequel film, Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.240
After doing her part in the&nbsp;
final battle against Thanos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:27.440
Valkyrie returns to New Asgard, where Thor tells&nbsp;
her that he's leaving and likely won't return.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:32.720
When she reminds him that his people need a king,&nbsp;
Thor informs her that they already have one.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.160
Just like that, Valkyrie is&nbsp;
handed the leadership of Asgard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.320
While that seems like a pretty happy ending,&nbsp;
it's important to remember the current state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:44.080
of the kingdom that she's been tasked&nbsp;
with ruling. The surviving Asgardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.160
lost their home planet and many of their&nbsp;
countrymen following Thanos' slaughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.800
The population of New Asgard is barely large&nbsp;
enough to fill a town, and it seems a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:58.080
unfair for Thor to ditch out and leave all his&nbsp;
kingly responsibilities to his second-in-command.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:03.200
Nevertheless, if anyone can turn things&nbsp;
around for the New Asgardians, it's Valkyrie.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.440
"You know I'd make a lot of changes around here."

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.400
"I'm counting on it."

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.360
Sam Wilson and Bucky Barnes wind up&nbsp;
sharing their final Endgame scene.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:13.920
After a dramatic entrance into the final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.520
Wilson and Barnes help hold back Thanos' armies&nbsp;
until Stark is finally able to finish them off.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:23.760
From there, the two heroes attend Stark's&nbsp;
funeral before they head off to witness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.440
Professor Hulk send Captain America back in time&nbsp;
to return the borrowed Infinity Stones. When Steve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:34.640
Rogers fails to return from the Quantum Realm,&nbsp;
Sam is concerned, but Bucky smiles knowingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.800
the first to understand Steve's choice&nbsp;
to remain in the past. Moments later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.160
when old Steve arrives with his shield in tow,&nbsp;
Bucky graciously steps aside to let Wilson take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.160 --> 00:05:49.440
up Cap's shield. As for Sam, he's honored when&nbsp;
Steve passes the Captain America mantle to him.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:54.640
"Thank you. I'll do my best."

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.800
It's a satisfying conclusion for&nbsp;
their Infinity Saga storylines,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:03.200
and a great setup for their own spinoff&nbsp;
storyline in The Falcon and the Winter Soldier.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:09.200
When we first meet the gentle giant, Professor&nbsp;
Hulk, it seems like a great new start to an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:13.200
exciting storyline for Bruce Banner and&nbsp;
his alter ego. But then the Professor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.920
Hulk narrative just kind of stalls out. While&nbsp;
he's pretty heavily involved in the time heist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:22.560
his character arc doesn't really go anywhere.&nbsp;
His biggest moment is reversing the Snap.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:27.760
"It's like, uh… I was made for this."

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:32.480
The problem is that Endgame was&nbsp;
supposed to be Hulk's chance to shine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.200
Banner and the Big Green Guy were at odds&nbsp;
throughout Infinity War, and it seemed like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:42.160
Endgame should've offered Hulk an opportunity to&nbsp;
redeem himself in battle, but it never quite came.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.600
While Scott Lang's involvement in Endgame&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:49.600
definitely pushes the plot forward&nbsp;
by bringing time travel to the table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:55.200
not much happens with the character himself. Hope&nbsp;
van Dyne's role in the movie is even smaller since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:59.760
she doesn't appear until the final battle. So&nbsp;
while the pair's endings in Endgame aren't bad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:04.880
they are fairly vanilla. The most they do in&nbsp;
the final battle is help repair Luis' van,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.880 --> 00:07:09.280
although that still turns out to be a dead&nbsp;
end. Afterward, we see them back home watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:14.240
fireworks with a teenage Cassie, and they're last&nbsp;
shown attending Stark's funeral. While the heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.680
undoubtedly have a bright future moving forward,&nbsp;
their Endgame endings aren't particularly special.

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:24.720
After spending the first act of Endgame&nbsp;
ruthlessly hunting down organized crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:29.360
syndicates and grieving the loss of his family,&nbsp;
Clint Barton attempts to find redemption during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.920
the time heist. He tries to sacrifice&nbsp;
himself to gain the final Infinity Stone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:38.480
but is instead forced to watch his best&nbsp;
friend, Natasha Romanoff, die in his place.

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:39.120
"Let me go."

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.120
"No. Please, no."

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:49.840
Clint eventually rediscovers his heroic&nbsp;
roots, and spends the final battle working&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:54.480
to get the Infinity Gauntlet to safety.&nbsp;
Following his appearance at Stark's funeral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.040
Clint is last seen sharing a quiet moment&nbsp;
with Wanda Maximoff as they both remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.520
their lost loved ones. The scene provides&nbsp;
some nice closure for the Infinity Saga&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.000
and sets the stage for each of the pair's&nbsp;
solo spinoff series, but is dampened a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.840
if you recall Clint's dark and violent&nbsp;
actions in the first half of the film.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.160
After being willing to sacrifice&nbsp;
everything she had in order to defeat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:20.800
Thanos at the end of Infinity War, Wanda&nbsp;
Maximoff returns thirsty for vengeance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:25.280
at the end of Endgame. And who can blame&nbsp;
her; thanks to Thanos' destructive actions,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:30.800
Wanda had to kill Vision, whom she loved... only&nbsp;
to then be forced to watch Thanos kill him again.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:35.120
The Scarlet Witch takes on Thanos mano&nbsp;
a mano in the final battle of Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:38.320
and likely would have killed him if&nbsp;
he hadn't been willing to destroy his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.800
own troops in order to stop her. Later,&nbsp;
she finds some peace talking to Hawkeye,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.920
finding comfort in her belief that Vision and&nbsp;
Natasha know their sacrifices weren't in vain.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:55.440
"She knows. They both do."

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.040
Despite being dusted for most of the movie,&nbsp;
Stephen Strange paves the way for the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:05.840
of Endgame by having willingly surrendered&nbsp;
the Time Stone at the end of Infinity War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:10.880
Although Strange gets snapped moments later,&nbsp;
his action steers the surviving Avengers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:14.560
toward their one-in-14 million&nbsp;
chance at a victorious outcome.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:18.880
Once he's brought back to life by Professor&nbsp;
Hulk's snap, Strange and his fellow Masters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:24.000
of the Mystic Arts open up numerous portals,&nbsp;
enabling thousands of heroic troops to join&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:27.920
the battle. Then, right when it seems&nbsp;
as though Thanos' victory is inevitable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:32.000
Strange finally reveals to Stark that&nbsp;
they are, indeed, operating within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:37.360
that one-in-14-million timeline. We last see&nbsp;
Strange paying his respects at Tony's funeral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:41.280
leaving him in a prime position to continue&nbsp;
playing a critical role in Phase 4.

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:46.960
For all intents and purposes, Gamora shouldn't&nbsp;
have had an ending in Endgame at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:50.160
But it turned out that the&nbsp;
2014 version of the heroine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:55.280
ultimately becomes the replacement for&nbsp;
the 2018 Gamora who died in Infinity War.

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:00.160
After jumping forward in time, Gamora turns on&nbsp;
her adoptive father during the final battle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:05.360
and is present for Stark's death. In a deleted&nbsp;
Endgame scene, it was revealed that afterward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:10.640
the confused 2014 version of the character&nbsp;
departs quietly for destinations unknown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:15.200
This open-ended finale is a fun one,&nbsp;
mostly because of how unexpected it is.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:21.040
With the universe at stake, the noble King&nbsp;
T'Challa is the first to step through Strange's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.560
portals. He joins the battle with Shuri, Okoye,&nbsp;
and a host of Wakandan soldiers at his back.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:32.400
In the ensuing conflict, the Wakandan armies&nbsp;
play a critical role in resisting Thanos' hordes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.640
with T'Challa even helping to keep&nbsp;
the Stark Gauntlet safe from Thanos.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:41.120
After the fight, the king and his country&nbsp;
can be seen reveling in their reunification&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:44.480
before T'Challa, Shuri, and&nbsp;
Okoye attend Stark's funeral.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.480
While T'Challa's final moments in&nbsp;
Endgame aren't particularly flashy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:52.160
they ended up being the last scenes that&nbsp;
actor Chadwick Boseman filmed for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:57.120
role before he tragically passed away. This&nbsp;
makes those scenes especially significant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:00.800
serving as Boseman's unexpected&nbsp;
farewell to the MCU as a whole.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.680
While Gamora's final moments in&nbsp;
Endgame are somewhat bittersweet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:10.240
the rest of the Guardians of the Galaxy have&nbsp;
happier endings. Rocket and Groot finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:15.600
reunite after five years apart, Star-Lord finds&nbsp;
hope in the fact that Gamora is still alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:19.760
and Drax and Mantis continue to provide&nbsp;
moments of unintentional hilarity.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:23.920
The best part of the Guardians of the Galaxy's&nbsp;
Endgame ending, though, is that it turned out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:29.440
not to be the last time we'd see the team working&nbsp;
together. Just months before Endgame hit theaters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:34.960
the long-derailed third Guardians installment got&nbsp;
back on track, with original director James Gunn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.320
back at the helm. This allowed the Endgame writers&nbsp;
to weave the future of the Guardians into Endgame,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:45.200
culminating in the scene where the Guardians are&nbsp;
preparing to leave Earth with Thor to find Gamora.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:48.800
The excitement of their reunions, as&nbsp;
well as the humor of their departure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.680
ranks as one of the better&nbsp;
multi-character endings in the film.

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:57.120
Thor goes through the wringer in Infinity&nbsp;
War, and seems to hit rock bottom in Endgame.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.040
But after some much-needed inspiration&nbsp;
from his mother during the time heist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:06.640
he finally reclaims some of his lost confidence.&nbsp;
After that, the son of Odin resumes his god-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:12.640
ways, wielding both Mjolnir and Stormbreaker&nbsp;
in his electrifying fight against Thanos.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:17.440
After the defeat of the Mad Titan, Thor spends&nbsp;
his final moments of Endgame passing off his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:21.280
kingly duties to Valkyrie and joining&nbsp;
up with the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.920
"Well, the Asgardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy, back together again."

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:30.000
Thor is last seen subtly challenging&nbsp;
Star-Lord for leadership,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.480
ending Endgame on a fun note for his character.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.280
The conflicted daughter of Thanos is&nbsp;
actually featured twice in Avengers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:41.760
Endgame, and both Nebulas receive solid&nbsp;
endings. The primary Nebula wraps up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:46.160
her journey by helping in the climactic&nbsp;
battle, attending Tony Stark's funeral,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.920
and then joining the Guardians of the&nbsp;
Galaxy. The former villain's redemptive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:54.880
journey is full of promise, with her dark past&nbsp;
literally left in ashes on the battlefield.

00:12:54.880 --> 00:13:00.720
However, 2014 Nebula's ending is less positive,&nbsp;
though still moving. She spends the majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:05.600
the movie tragically tethered to father's every&nbsp;
whim, bringing the Sanctuary II through the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:10.240
machine and nearly killing Hawkeye in her&nbsp;
attempt to reclaim the Infinity Gauntlet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:15.120
At that moment, Gamora and the other Nebula&nbsp;
arrive and attempt to talk her out of the deed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:20.160
Unable to change, she's eventually shot and&nbsp;
killed by her older self. A tear runs down her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:24.640
cheek as she dies, bringing a heartbreaking&nbsp;
ending to a deeply conflicted character.

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:31.280
Original Avenger Natasha Romanoff's character&nbsp;
arc is shockingly cut short in Endgame. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:35.760
she's the only one on the list whose ending&nbsp;
wraps up before the third act of the film.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:40.320
Up until this point, Romanoff's MCU&nbsp;
journey has always been one of redemption.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:44.720
Starting with red in her ledger, the super&nbsp;
spy consistently worked to make amends for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:49.920
her past in her MCU appearances throughout&nbsp;
the Infinity Saga. Her story abruptly ended&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:54.640
when she sacrificed herself to get the Soul&nbsp;
Stone halfway through Endgame. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:59.280
Natasha's universe-saving sacrifice becomes&nbsp;
one of Endgame's most powerful endings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:02.960
even if it meant she wasn't around to&nbsp;
participate in the film's grand finale.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:04.613
"It's okay."

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:10.720
While most of the best endings in Endgame belong&nbsp;
to heroes, Thanos scores highly on the list by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:16.480
receiving two satisfying endings. The 2018 version&nbsp;
of the villain meets his end early on in the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:19.520
when he's hunted down by the&nbsp;
Avengers and decapitated by Thor.

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:22.080
"I went for the head."

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:26.720
This is actually closest to the ending Thanos&nbsp;
wanted. Not only does he wipe out half of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:31.520
the universe, but he prevents his victory from&nbsp;
being undone by destroying the Infinity Stones.

00:14:31.520 --> 00:14:35.040
But he never could have predicted&nbsp;
that the Avengers will go back in time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:38.080
to walk back his success. During the time heist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:43.920
2014 Thanos emerges as the Avengers' ultimate&nbsp;
foe once again. This leads to his final ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:47.280
in which he and his armies are&nbsp;
poetically snapped away into the wind.

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:53.200
Captain America's story arc stretches nearly&nbsp;
the entire length of the Infinity Saga before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:58.640
it finally comes full circle in Endgame.&nbsp;
Steve Rogers' path begins during World War II,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:03.760
when he's transformed from a 90-pound weakling&nbsp;
into a super soldier of epic proportions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:06.960
His journey eventually catapults&nbsp;
him into the 21st century,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.600
where he becomes a founding&nbsp;
member of the Avengers.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:14.960
By Endgame, Cap has evolved from patriotic&nbsp;
soldier to universe-saving team leader,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:19.600
and his final act includes several moments&nbsp;
that fans waited nearly a decade to see.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:27.520
"Avengers, assemble."

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:33.440
From that long-awaited line to his opportunity to&nbsp;
finally wield Mjolnir in battle, Endgame is full&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:38.800
of opportunities for Steve to shine. Ultimately,&nbsp;
though, it's his chance to go back in time and get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:44.160
that dance with Peggy Carter that truly feels&nbsp;
like the ending he deserves. After a lifetime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:49.040
spent feeling out of place and at the service of&nbsp;
others, Steve finally gets a life for himself.

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:54.160
"How'd that work out for you?"

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:54.960
"It was beautiful."

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.720
The entire Marvel Cinematic Universe kicks off&nbsp;
with Tony Stark's pivot from a narcissistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:05.840
playboy into a bona fide superhero. Early in&nbsp;
his journey, Tony proves that he's willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:10.240
sacrifice himself for the greater good when&nbsp;
he flies a nuke into space and hurls it at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:15.200
a Chitauri ship. When he survives, the next&nbsp;
several years see an anxious Stark doing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:21.040
best to prepare for the next world-ending threat,&nbsp;
only to still fail when he faces Thanos on Titan.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.680
In Endgame, though, he gets a second shot at&nbsp;
saving the world. After realizing that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:30.640
one version of reality where they win can&nbsp;
only be achieved by sacrificing himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:35.120
he doesn't hesitate. Stark snaps away&nbsp;
every last one of Thanos' soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.360
knowing it means he'll never see his family again.

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:46.080
"I am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:46.720
Iron Man."

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:50.560
The heroic act marks the end&nbsp;
of the World's Greatest Hero,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:55.040
but his selfless sacrifice makes it&nbsp;
the best character ending in the film.

00:16:55.040 --> 00:16:55.680
"I love you 3000."

